 data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 122 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 27.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.5, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.5 to 5.7. December accounts for 12% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 10% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 96 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,800 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar patterns can occur due to seasonal demand or budget cycles. The number of awardees does not prove any single contract was invalid or improperly awarded.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts awarded in December for consistency with the body’s needs. Verify if multiple contracts for the same service were awarded to different awardees. Review the terms of contract [1] to ensure compliance with the legal limit.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["B7Veys4eeVPmnwcj%2BxbdTg%3D%3D","qvmCc%2BjP%2BSwZDGvgaZEVxQ%3D%3D","fn0xe5hcgHSIzo3LHNPGcQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}